{title: Rejoice Forever}
{subtitle: Psalms 5:12}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]LORD lead me in your [Eb]righteousness
[Gm7]Make your way straight be[Eb]fore me
[Bb]There is [Eb]nothing trustworthy in their [Gm7]mouth
Within them [Eb]is destruc[Gm7]tion
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Their throat is [Eb]an open grave
[Gm7]With their tongues they flat[Eb]ter
[Gm7]Declare [Eb]them guilty God
[Cm7]Let them fall [Bb/D]by their [Eb]own schemes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]But let all who [Eb]take refuge [Gm7]in you re[F]joice
Let them [Bb]sing for joy forev[Eb]er
Spread your shelter o[Gm7]ver them
Let those who love [F]your name exult in [Bb]you [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]For you have rebelled [Eb]against him
[Gm7]Drive them out for their [Eb]many transgressions
[Bb]But the righteous find [Eb]a steady rest
In the [Gm7]presence of the [Eb]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]But let all who [Eb]take refuge [Gm7]in you re[F]joice
Let them [Bb]sing for joy forev[Eb]er
Spread your shelter o[Gm7]ver them
Let those who love [F]your name exult in you [Eb][F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]You surround them with fa[F]vor
As with a [Gm7]shield [Bbmaj7/D]
[Eb]The blessing of the [F]LORD rests
Up[Gm7]on the right[Bbmaj7/F]eous [Eb]heart
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Sing for [Eb]joy forev[Gm7]er
[F]Exult in [Bb]you
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
